  significance against the framework: naive +6.84 sigma  ->  fully corrected +3.70 sigma
  significance against LambdaCDM (predicts exactly 0): +1.71 sigma, unchanged by any of this
  [PASS] A1 the corrected treatment SUPPRESSES the predicted slope, because these dwarfs' internal fields are comparable to their external ones so nu responds only weakly to the environment   (naive -0.2394 -> corrected -0.0929 (suppression factor 2.58))
  [PASS] A2 AGAINST THE FRAMEWORK'S INTEREST, and the point of the script: the suppression does NOT dissolve the negative, because the disagreement is one of SIGN.  The observed slope is POSITIVE and the corrected prediction is still NEGATIVE, and no coupling correction can fix a sign   (corrected prediction -0.0929 vs observed +0.0800 +- 0.0467: still +3.70 sigma against the framework, while LambdaCDM's exact zero sits +1.71 sigma away and gets the sign right)

