================================================================================================================
VERDICT
================================================================================================================
  The prediction side of the ~5 sigma external-field negative has been recomputed with both of this programme's own
  prescription errors fixed, and THE NEGATIVE SURVIVES.  Including the dwarfs' internal fields in nu's argument does
  suppress the predicted slope, and by more than f01's sphere-average term, because these systems have internal fields
  comparable to their external ones.  But the corrected prediction remains NEGATIVE while the measurement is POSITIVE:
  the disagreement is a SIGN disagreement, and no correction to a coupling can fix a sign.  LambdaCDM predicts exactly
  zero by the strong equivalence principle and sits closer to the data on both footings.
  This CLOSES the caveat I attached to the liability table twice today.  The external-field negative is not an artefact
  of the programme's prescription errors and must be read as a real result.

